        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: کونا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کونا — konā — \"a corner\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کونا (konā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from koṇa, \"corner, angle\" (CDIAL 3504). CDIAL, after Burrow, takes the Sanskrit word from Dravidian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
